1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,244
This girl fell three

2
00:00:01,244 --> 00:00:02,730
kilometers out of the sky,

3
00:00:02,730 --> 00:00:03,920
still strapped to her seat.

4
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:05,220
And she survived.

5
00:00:05,670 --> 00:00:08,120
On Christmas Eve, 1971,

6
00:00:08,670 --> 00:00:09,625
seventeen-year-old

7
00:00:09,625 --> 00:00:11,099
Juliane Koepcke was flying

8
00:00:11,099 --> 00:00:13,010
over the Amazon with her mother.

9
00:00:13,410 --> 00:00:15,210
Then the plane flew into a thunderstorm.

10
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:16,600
Lightning struck,

11
00:00:16,910 --> 00:00:18,370
and it broke apart in mid-air.

12
00:00:18,820 --> 00:00:20,930
She woke up on the jungle floor, alone.

13
00:00:21,590 --> 00:00:23,000
Her collarbone was broken,

14
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:24,270
and her mother was gone.

15
00:00:24,670 --> 00:00:26,450
All she had was a small bag of candy.

16
00:00:26,900 --> 00:00:28,790
But she remembered her father's advice.

17
00:00:29,160 --> 00:00:30,450
Find water, and follow it.

18
00:00:30,750 --> 00:00:31,896
So she followed a stream,

19
00:00:31,896 --> 00:00:33,590
then a river. For days.

20
00:00:34,090 --> 00:00:35,950
Maggots got into a wound on her arm.

21
00:00:36,450 --> 00:00:37,405
On the tenth day,

22
00:00:37,405 --> 00:00:38,660
she found a boat, and fuel.

23
00:00:39,170 --> 00:00:40,670
She poured it on the wound,

24
00:00:40,670 --> 00:00:41,830
to drive the maggots out.

25
00:00:42,280 --> 00:00:43,630
Then, lumberjacks found her.

26
00:00:44,060 --> 00:00:45,470
They thought she was a water spirit.

27
00:00:45,870 --> 00:00:47,230
She was the only survivor,

28
00:00:47,570 --> 00:00:48,880
out of ninety-two people.

29
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:51,100
Today, she's a biologist,

30
00:00:51,520 --> 00:00:53,021
and runs a research station

31
00:00:53,021 --> 00:00:54,300
in that same rainforest.
